    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Calculating the volume and pore volume of a node-centered control volume.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Philipp Weis, ETH Zuerich </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1contact">
<title>Contact</title><para><ulink url="mailto:philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch">philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch</ulink></para>
<para>@changes changes Latest Changes</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1motivation">
<title>Motivation</title><para>Intitially designed to avoid the usage of the FiniteVolumeManager in csp5. Output as nodal field variables allows to use them for post-processing (e.g. with ParaView or MatLab).</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1usage">
<title>Usage</title><para>Used within the CVFEM scheme (Weis et al., Geofluids, 2014).</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>visitor<sp/>reads<sp/>in<sp/>a<sp/>nodal<sp/>variable<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">for</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>porosity,<sp/>which<sp/>has<sp/>to<sp/>be<sp/>initialised<sp/>before<sp/>visitation</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">It<sp/>further<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">requires</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>existing<sp/>nodal<sp/>variables<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">for</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>volume<sp/>and<sp/>pore<sp/>volume.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>three<sp/>variable<sp/>names<sp/>are<sp/>provided<sp/>as<sp/>constructor<sp/>arguments.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>The<sp/>visitor<sp/>calculates<sp/>the<sp/>node-centered<sp/>volume<sp/>and<sp/>pore<sp/>volume,<sp/>assuming<sp/>that<sp/>all<sp/>elements<sp/>contribute<sp/>equally<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>control<sp/>volumes<sp/>of<sp/>their<sp/>respecetive<sp/>nodes.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>values<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">for</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>volume<sp/>and<sp/>pore<sp/>volume<sp/>are<sp/>stored<sp/>as<sp/>nodal<sp/>variables.</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1dependencies">
<title>Dependencies</title></sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1issues">
<title>Known issues</title><para>There may be new funcionality in CSMP++ that could make this visitor redundant. Only <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_pore_volume_visitor_1a13736ab4ca7daef2bf7aaa66a338ef8b" kindref="member">Visit(Node&lt;dim&gt;* n)</ref> is overwritten. However, application target and level are always set to NODE. How to limit to <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_region" kindref="compound">Region</ref> (former Group)?</para>
<para>Does the Application Level have to be changed? How can it be restricted to a <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_region" kindref="compound">Region</ref>? Include the possibility to use porosity as an element variable? Change name to NodalPoreVolumeVisitor?</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1testing">
<title>Testing</title><para>testing was done in the period before publication in 2014. </para>
</sect1>
